d><td>65</td><td>79.6%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/the-netherlands-in-numbers-2026-minimum.html\">Netherlands</a></td><td>$2,617</td><td>27.9%</td><td>3.91%</td><td>$0.27</td><td>+16%</td><td>67</td><td>96%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/new-zealand-in-numbers-2026-minimum.html\">New Zealand</a></td><td>$2,361</td><td>20.8%</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>65 (NZ Super)</td><td>43.8%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/norway-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage-tax.html\">Norway</a></td><td>None</td><td>28.1%</td><td>—</td><td>$0.22</td><td>—</td><td>67</td><td>54.9%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/poland-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage-tax.html\">Poland</a></td><td>$1,252</td><td>24.4%</td><td>—</td><td>$0.34</td><td>+13.3%</td><td>65 men / 60 women</td><td>40.6%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/portugal-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">Portugal</a></td><td>$1,201</td><td>24.9%</td><td>3.03%</td><td>$0.27</td><td>+24.5%</td><td>66 y 9 m</td><td>92.7%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/slovakia-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">Slovakia</a></td><td>$1,024</td><td>24.3%</td><td>3.73%</td><td>$0.22</td><td>+27.9%</td><td>—</td><td>76.3%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/slovenia-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage.html\">Slovenia</a></td><td>$1,659</td><td>36.2%</td><td>3.22%</td><td>$0.24</td><td>+23.3%</td><td>—</td><td>71.3%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/south-africa-in-numbers-2026-minimum.html\">South Africa</a></td><td>$316</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>60 (Older Persons Grant)</td><td>8.9%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/south-korea-in-numbers-2026-minimum.html\">South Korea</a></td><td>$1,351</td><td>16.5%</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>63</td><td>38.9%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/spain-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage-tax.html\">Spain</a></td><td>$1,595</td><td>23.5%</td><td>3.04%</td><td>$0.28</td><td>+21%</td><td>66 y 10 m</td><td>86.3%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/sweden-in-numbers-2026-minimum-wage-tax.html\">Sweden</a></td><td>None</td><td>22.6%</td><td>—</td><td>$0.34</td><td>+14.4%</td><td>67 (guarantee pension)</td><td>66.3%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/switzerland-in-numbers-2026-tax.html\">Switzerland</a></td><td>—</td><td>18.1%</td><td>1.1%</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>65 men / 64 y 6 m women</td><td>47.5%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/the-united-kingdom-in-numbers-2026.html\">United Kingdom</a></td><td>$2,945</td><td>23.1%</td><td>6%</td><td>$0.35</td><td>+32.5%</td><td>66, rising to 67</td><td>54.2%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/the-united-states-in-numbers-2026.html\">United States</a></td><td>$1,257</td><td>24.3%</td><td>7.32%</td><td>$0.18</td><td>+45.9%</td><td>67</td><td>51.3%</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<p><small>\"None\": no statutory minimum wage (collective agreements). \"—\": not in that dataset.</small></p>\n\n<h2 id=\"downloads\">Download the Data</h2>\n<p>Every table behind these pages is free to download as a CSV file and reuse with credit to Blog Digest (CC BY 4.0):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@ccr-ee047f91-rbyv4x/seo/data/minimum-wage-2026.csv\">Minimum wage 2026</a> (from <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/minimum-wage-by-country-2026-hourly-and.html\">Minimum Wage by Country 2026: Hourly and Monthly Rates in US Dollars</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@ccr-ee047f91-rbyv4x/seo/data/take-home-pay-average-wage-2025.csv\">Take home pay average wage 2025</a> (from <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/income-tax-by-country-2026-how-much-of.html\">Income Tax by Country 2026: How Much of Your Salary You Keep in 38 Countries</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@ccr-ee047f91-rbyv4x/seo/data/mortgage-rates-2026.csv\">Mortgage rates 2026</a> (from <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/mortgage-rates-by-country-2026-where.html\">Mortgage Rates by Country 2026: Where Buying a Home Costs the Most</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@ccr-ee047f91-rbyv4x/seo/data/household-electricity-prices-2026.csv\">Household electricity prices 2026</a> (from <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/electricity-prices-by-country-2026-what.html\">Electricity Prices by Country 2026: What Households Pay per kWh, and What the Iran War Means for Bills</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@ccr-ee047f91-rbyv4x/seo/data/petrol-prices-since-feb-2026.csv\">Petrol prices since feb 2026</a> (from <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/petrol-prices-since-iran-war-how-much.html\">Petrol Prices Since the Iran War: How Much They Have Risen in 35 Countries</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@ccr-ee047f91-rbyv4x/seo/data/retirement-age-2026.csv\">Retirement age 2026</a> (from <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/retirement-age-by-country-2026-state.html\">Retirement Age by Country 2026: State Pension Ages in 39 Countries</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@ccr-ee047f91-rbyv4x/seo/data/pension-net-replacement-rates.csv\">Pension net replacement rates</a> (from <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/state-pension-amounts-by-country-2026.html\">State Pension Amounts by Country 2026: How Much Retirees Actually Get</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@ccr-ee047f91-rbyv4x/seo/data/deposit-insurance-limits-2026.csv\">Deposit insurance limits 2026</a> (from <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/deposit-insurance-limits-by-country.html\">Deposit Insurance Limits by Country 2026: How Much of Your Money Is Protected</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@ccr-ee047f91-rbyv4x/seo/data/inheritance-tax-2026.csv\">Inheritance tax 2026</a> (from <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/inheritance-tax-by-country-2026.html\">Inheritance Tax by Country 2026: Thresholds, Rates and Who Pays</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@ccr-ee047f91-rbyv4x/seo/data/retirement-visa-income-rules-2026.csv\">Retirement visa income rules 2026</a> (from <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/best-countries-to-retire-abroad-on-2000.html\">Best Countries to Retire Abroad on $2,000 a Month: Costs, Visas and Taxes Compared</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/venkateshramu07-design/My_Repo@ccr-ee047f91-rbyv4x/seo/data/salary-increase-forecasts-2027.csv\">Salary increase forecasts 2027</a> (from <a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/salary-increase-forecasts-2027-by.html\">Salary Increase Forecasts 2027 by Country: Every Major Survey in One Table</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>How to Use These Comparisons</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Wages and tax together:</strong> a high minimum wage can come with high tax. Compare the US-dollar minimum wage with the share of pay the average worker keeps.</li>\n<li><strong>Homes:</strong> the mortgage rate sets the monthly payment. A 2-point difference adds about 20% to the payment on a 25-year loan.</li>\n<li><strong>Bills:</strong> electricity prices vary more than threefold. Petrol rises since February show where the Iran war hit hardest.</li>\n<li><strong>Retirement:</strong> look at the pension age and the share of pay the pension replaces together; a later age with a generous pension can beat an early age with a small one.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n<h3>Which country has the highest minimum wage in 2026?</h3>\n<p>Converted to US dollars for a month of full-time work, the highest minimum wages are in Luxembourg, Australia and the United Kingdom.</p>\n<h3>Which country takes the most tax from an average worker?</h3>\n<p>Counting income tax and employee social security on the average wage, the highest are Belgium, Germany and Lithuania; the lowest are Mexico, South Korea and Switzerland.</p>\n<h3>Where are mortgage rates lowest?</h3>\n<p>Among these countries, the lowest typical mortgage rates are in Switzerland, Japan and Portugal.</p>\n<h3>Which country has the cheapest electricity?</h3>\n<p>The cheapest household electricity, in US dollars per kWh, is in the United States, Slovakia and Norway.</p>\n<h3>Where is the retirement age lowest?</h3>\n<p>The lowest state pension ages among these countries are in India, South Africa and China.</p>\n\n<div class=\"bd-cite\" style=\"margin:1.6em 0;padding:14px 16px;border-radius:14px;border:1px solid rgba(120,120,140,.25);font:500 14px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif\"><b>Cite this page:</b> Blog Digest, &ldquo;Minimum Wage by Country 2026: Tax, Mortgage Rates, Energy and Pension Age in 35 Countries&rdquo;, updated 25 October 2026, https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/compare-countries-2026-minimum-wage-tax.html</div>\n<h2>Related Guides</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/minimum-wage-by-country-2026-hourly-and.html\">Minimum Wage by Country 2026: Hourly and Monthly Rates in US Dollars</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/income-tax-by-country-2026-how-much-of.html\">Income Tax by Country 2026: How Much of Your Salary You Keep in 38 Countries</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/mortgage-rates-by-country-2026-where.html\">Mortgage Rates by Country 2026: Where Buying a Home Costs the Most</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/electricity-prices-by-country-2026-what.html\">Electricity Prices by Country 2026: What Households Pay per kWh, and What the Iran War Means for Bills</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/petrol-prices-since-iran-war-how-much.html\">Petrol Prices Since the Iran War: How Much They Have Risen in 35 Countries</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/retirement-age-by-country-2026-state.html\">Retirement Age by Country 2026: State Pension Ages in 39 Countries</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/state-pension-amounts-by-country-2026.html\">State Pension Amounts by Country 2026: How Much Retirees Actually Get</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/deposit-insurance-limits-by-country.html\">Deposit Insurance Limits by Country 2026: How Much of Your Money Is Protected</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/inheritance-tax-by-country-2026.html\">Inheritance Tax by Country 2026: Thresholds, Rates and Who Pays</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/best-countries-to-retire-abroad-on-2000.html\">Best Countries to Retire Abroad on $2,000 a Month: Costs, Visas and Taxes Compared</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2026/10/salary-increase-forecasts-2027-by.html\">Salary Increase Forecasts 2027 by Country: Every Major Survey in One Table</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>Figures from the official sources listed in each linked guide, checked in October 2026. Exchange-rate conversions are approximate. For information only; not financial advice.</em></p>\n\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\" id=\"bd-faq-ld\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Which country has the highest minimum wage in 2026?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Converted to US dollars for a month of full-time work, the highest minimum wages are in Luxembourg, Australia and the United Kingdom.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Which country takes the most tax from an average worker?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Counting income tax and employee social security on the average wage, the highest are Belgium, Germany and Lithuania; the lowest are Mexico, South Korea and Switzerland.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Where are mortgage rates lowest?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Among these countries, the lowest typical mortgage rates are in Switzerland, Japan and Portugal.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Which country has the cheapest electricity?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"The cheapest household electricity, in US dollars per kWh, is in the United States, Slovakia and Norway.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Where is the retirement age lowest?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"The lowest state pension ages among these countries are in India, South Africa and China.\"}}]}</script>\n</div>",
